Fillets: patch 1140's end past the spine's end vertex not where the face
of the other contact, Fo, is closed round its surface (mitcad#1336).

The case: a pin of radius 4.5 standing on a plate's top, flush with the
plate's end, a half round of the pin's radius whose sides are tangent to
the pin; the pin's cylinder and that end are one face, closed round the
axis. The pin's foot on the top is rounded with 1 along its arc of 302
degrees, between the two tangent points V1 and V2, where the sides start.
The rounding's contact on the top leaves it across the sides' edges with
the top, and the sides cut the blend (ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd); the other
contact's line on the pin, Fo, meets the side's edge with the pin, Eq,
only beyond V, along Eq's line up the pin. Patch 1140 (and 1170) took that
end past V there and prolonged Eq beyond V. But the other contact's line
is a closed circle: the analytic piece's parameters at its ends were the
whole line's, a period apart (each end's section on the line at the
period's end, the last one at the start), so the pieces cut from it ran the
wrong way round; and at V2 Eq's line beyond V is the pin's seam, which Eq
was prolonged over. The result was not valid (two tori, one inside out, or
an unorientable face), where before patch 1140 the corner (PerformOneCorner,
OnSame, patch 0911) cut both ends by the sides, which grow up to the
rounding, as the stored design's body has it.

Now the end past V is not taken where Fo has a seam (an edge closed on
it): the corner closes such an end as before patch 1140. Every case of
patches 1140 and 1170 (a floor, a wall and a corner's cylinder, none closed
round its surface) builds as before.

On the stored design's body before the item (a pin on a plate's rounded
end, rounded with 1): valid, one torus, the material added 4.76572 against
the file's 4.76602 mm3 (patch 0911's result), where the end past V made an
invalid shape. Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_tangent_end_face.cpp, the
pin on a plate's end whose seam runs along a side at V2: valid, one torus,
the material added within 1e-6 of the ring at the foot within the sides'
planes (without the patch: not valid, two tori).

Upstream: new.

